    {
      "name": "DEPLOYMENT.md",
      "type": "documentation",
      "path": "docs/DEPLOYMENT.md",
      "size": 16384,
      "description": "Comprehensive deployment guide for AWS ECS Fargate",
      "dependencies": [],
      "content": "=== docs/DEPLOYMENT.md ===\n# Deployment Guide - Mini Java App on AWS ECS Fargate\n\n## Table of Contents\n1. [Prerequisites](#prerequisites)\n2. [Project Overview](#project-overview)\n3. [Local Development Setup](#local-development-setup)\n4. [Building and Testing Locally](#building-and-testing-locally)\n5. [AWS ECS Fargate Prerequisites](#aws-ecs-fargate-prerequisites)\n6. [Container Registry Setup](#container-registry-setup)\n7. [Building and Pushing Docker Image](#building-and-pushing-docker-image)\n8. [ECS Task Definition Explained](#ecs-task-definition-explained)\n9. [ECS Service Configuration](#ecs-service-configuration)\n10. [Deploying to AWS ECS Fargate](#deploying-to-aws-ecs-fargate)\n11. [Post-Deployment Verification](#post-deployment-verification)\n12. [Monitoring and Logging](#monitoring-and-logging)\n13. [Scaling and Management](#scaling-and-management)\n14. [Troubleshooting](#troubleshooting)\n15. [Security Best Practices](#security-best-practices)\n\n---\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n### Required Tools\n- **Java Development Kit (JDK) 11**: For building the application\n- **Maven 3.6+**: Build automation tool\n- **Docker 20.10+**: For containerization\n- **AWS CLI 2.x**: For AWS operations\n- **Git**: Version control\n\n### AWS Account Requirements\n- Active AWS account with appropriate permissions\n- AWS CLI configured with credentials\n- IAM permissions for ECS, ECR, VPC, CloudWatch, and IAM\n\n### Verify Installations\n\n```bash\n# Check Java version\njava -version\n\n# Check Maven version\nmvn -version\n\n# Check Docker version\ndocker --version\n\n# Check AWS CLI version\naws --version\n\n# Verify AWS credentials\naws sts get-caller-identity\n```\n\n---\n\n## Project Overview\n\n### Technology Stack\n- **Language**: Java 11\n- **Framework**: Spring Boot 2.7.0\n- **Build Tool**: Maven\n- **Package Type**: JAR\n- **Application Port**: 8080\n- **Context Path**: /mini-app\n\n### Application Architecture\n- **Type**: Web Application / Microservice\n- **Dependencies**: MySQL Connector, Spring Boot Starter Web\n- **External Services**: Database, Redis, RabbitMQ, External APIs\n\n### Key Features\n- Configuration file loading from `/app/config`\n- Logging to `/app/logs`\n- Environment variable configuration\n- Containerized for AWS ECS Fargate deployment\n\n---\n\n## Local Development Setup\n\n### 1. Clone the Repository\n\n```bash\ngit clone <repository-url>\ncd mini-java-app\n```\n\n### 2. Configure Application Properties\n\nEdit `src/main/resources/application.properties` to configure local settings:\n\n```properties\nserver.port=8080\nserver.host=0.0.0.0\nserver.context-path=/mini-app\n\n# Database configuration (point to local or remote database)\ndatabase.url=jdbc:mysql://localhost:3306/mini_app_db\ndatabase.username=root\ndatabase.password=password123\n\n# Redis configuration\ncache.redis.host=localhost\ncache.redis.port=6379\n\n# RabbitMQ configuration\nmessaging.rabbitmq.host=localhost\nmessaging.rabbitmq.port=5672\n```\n\n### 3. Build the Application\n\n```bash\nmvn clean package -DskipTests\n```\n\n### 4. Run Locally\n\n```bash\njava -jar target/mini-java-app-1.0.0.jar\n```\n\n### 5. Test the Application\n\n```bash\ncurl http://localhost:8080/mini-app\n```\n\n---\n\n## Building and Testing Locally\n\n### Build with Docker Compose\n\n```bash\n# Build and start the application\ndocker-compose up --build\n\n# Run in detached mode\ndocker-compose up -d\n\n# View logs\ndocker-compose logs -f\n\n# Stop the application\ndocker-compose down\n```\n\n### Test the Containerized Application\n\n```bash\n# Check if container is running\ndocker ps\n\n# Test the endpoint\ncurl http://localhost:8080/mini-app\n\n# View container logs\ndocker logs mini-java-app\n```\n\n---\n\n## AWS ECS Fargate Prerequisites\n\n### 1. VPC and Networking Setup\n\nECS Fargate requires a VPC with at least 2 subnets in different Availability Zones.\n\n```bash\n# List available VPCs\naws ec2 describe-vpcs --query 'Vpcs[*].[VpcId,CidrBlock,Tags[?Key==`Name`].Value|[0]]' --output table\n\n# List subnets in a VPC\naws ec2 describe-subnets --filters \"Name=vpc-id,Values=<vpc-id>\" --query 'Subnets[*].[SubnetId,AvailabilityZone,CidrBlock]' --output table\n```\n\n#### Create VPC (if needed)\n\n```bash\n# Create VPC\naws ec2 create-vpc --cidr-block 10.0.0.0/16\n\n# Create subnets in different AZs\naws ec2 create-subnet --vpc-id <vpc-id> --cidr-block 10.0.1.0/24 --availability-zone us-east-1a\naws ec2 create-subnet --vpc-id <vpc-id> --cidr-block 10.0.2.0/24 --availability-zone us-east-1b\n\n# Create Internet Gateway\naws ec2 create-internet-gateway\naws ec2 attach-internet-gateway --vpc-id <vpc-id> --internet-gateway-id <igw-id>\n\n# Create route table and associate with subnets\naws ec2 create-route-table --vpc-id <vpc-id>\naws ec2 create-route --route-table-id <rt-id> --destination-cidr-block 0.0.0.0/0 --gateway-id <igw-id>\naws ec2 associate-route-table --subnet-id <subnet-id> --route-table-id <rt-id>\n```\n\n### 2. Security Group Setup\n\nCreate a security group that allows inbound traffic on port 8080.\n\n```bash\n# Create security group\naws ec2 create-security-group \\\n  --group-name mini-java-app-sg \\\n  --description \"Security group for mini-java-app ECS tasks\" \\\n  --vpc-id <vpc-id>\n\n# Add inbound rule for application port\naws ec2 authorize-security-group-ingress \\\n  --group-id <sg-id> \\\n  --protocol tcp \\\n  --port 8080 \\\n  --cidr 0.0.0.0/0\n\n# Add inbound rule for HTTP (if using ALB)\naws ec2 authorize-security-group-ingress \\\n  --group-id <sg-id> \\\n  --protocol tcp \\\n  --port 80 \\\n  --cidr 0.0.0.0/0\n```\n\n### 3. IAM Roles Setup\n\n#### ECS Task Execution Role\n\nThis role allows ECS to pull images from ECR and write logs to CloudWatch.\n\n```bash\n# Create trust policy file\ncat > ecs-task-execution-trust-policy.json << EOF\n{\n  \"Version\": \"2012-10-17\",\n  \"Statement\": [\n    {\n      \"Effect\": \"Allow\",\n      \"Principal\": {\n        \"Service\": \"ecs-tasks.amazonaws.com\"\n      },\n      \"Action\": \"sts:AssumeRole\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\nEOF\n\n# Create the role\naws iam create-role \\\n  --role-name ecsTaskExecutionRole \\\n  --assume-role-policy-document file://ecs-task-execution-trust-policy.json\n\n# Attach AWS managed policy\naws iam attach-role-policy \\\n  --role-name ecsTaskExecutionRole \\\n  --policy-arn arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/service-role/AmazonECSTaskExecutionRolePolicy\n```\n\n#### ECS Task Role (Optional)\n\nThis role grants permissions to the application running in the container.\n\n```bash\n# Create the task role\naws iam create-role \\\n  --role-name ecsTaskRole \\\n  --assume-role-policy-document file://ecs-task-execution-trust-policy.json\n\n# Attach custom policies as needed (e.g., S3 access, DynamoDB access)\n```\n\n### 4. CloudWatch Log Group\n\n```bash\n# Create log group\naws logs create-log-group --log-group-name /ecs/mini-java-app\n\n# Set retention policy (optional)\naws logs put-retention-policy \\\n  --log-group-name /ecs/mini-java-app \\\n  --retention-in-days 7\n```\n\n---\n\n## Container Registry Setup\n\n### Option 1: AWS ECR (Recommended)\n\n#### Create ECR Repository\n\n```bash\n# Create repository\naws ecr create-repository --repository-name mini-java-app --region us-east-1\n\n# Get repository URI\naws ecr describe-repositories --repository-names mini-java-app --query 'repositories[0].repositoryUri' --output text\n```\n\n#### Authenticate Docker with ECR\n\n```bash\n# Get login password and authenticate\naws ecr get-login-password --region us-east-1 | docker login --username AWS --password-stdin <account-id>.dkr.ecr.us-east-1.amazonaws.com\n```\n\n### Option 2: Docker Hub\n\n```bash\n# Login to Docker Hub\ndocker login\n```\n\n---\n\n## Building and Pushing Docker Image\n\n### Using Build Script (Recommended)\n\n#### Linux/macOS:\n\n```bash\nchmod +x scripts/build-push.sh\n./scripts/build-push.sh\n```\n\n#### Windows:\n\n```cmd\nscripts\\build-push.bat\n```\n\n### Manual Build and Push\n\n```bash\n# Build the image\ndocker build -t mini-java-app:latest .\n\n# Tag for ECR\ndocker tag mini-java-app:latest <account-id>.dkr.ecr.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/mini-java-app:latest\n\n# Push to ECR\ndocker push <account-id>.dkr.ecr.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/mini-java-app:latest\n```\n\n---\n\n## ECS Task Definition Explained\n\n### Key Components\n\n#### 1. Launch Type and Resources\n\n```json\n\"requiresCompatibilities\": [\"FARGATE\"],\n\"networkMode\": \"awsvpc\",\n\"cpu\": \"512\",\n\"memory\": \"1024\"\n```\n\n**Valid Fargate CPU/Memory Combinations:**\n- CPU: 256 (.25 vCPU) → Memory: 512, 1024, 2048 MB\n- CPU: 512 (.5 vCPU) → Memory: 1024, 2048, 3072, 4096 MB\n- CPU: 1024 (1 vCPU) → Memory: 2048-8192 MB (increments of 1024)\n- CPU: 2048 (2 vCPU) → Memory: 4096-16384 MB\n- CPU: 4096 (4 vCPU) → Memory: 8192-30720 MB\n\n#### 2. IAM Roles\n\n```json\n\"executionRoleArn\": \"arn:aws:iam::<account-id>:role/ecsTaskExecutionRole\",\n\"taskRoleArn\": \"arn:aws:iam::<account-id>:role/ecsTaskRole\"\n```\n\n- **executionRoleArn**: Required for Fargate. Used by ECS agent to pull images and write logs.\n- **taskRoleArn**: Optional. Grants AWS permissions to the application code.\n\n#### 3. Container Definition\n\n```json\n\"containerDefinitions\": [\n  {\n    \"name\": \"mini-java-app\",\n    \"image\": \"<account-id>.dkr.ecr.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/mini-java-app:latest\",\n    \"essential\": true,\n    \"portMappings\": [{\"containerPort\": 8080, \"protocol\": \"tcp\"}],\n    \"environment\": [...],\n    \"logConfiguration\": {...}\n  }\n]\n```\n\n#### 4. Environment Variables\n\n```json\n\"environment\": [\n  {\"name\": \"SERVER_PORT\", \"value\": \"8080\"},\n  {\"name\": \"JAVA_OPTS\", \"value\": \"-Xmx512m -Xms256m\"},\n  {\"name\": \"DB_HOST\", \"value\": \"database.example.com\"},\n  {\"name\": \"CONFIG_DIR\", \"value\": \"/app/config\"}\n]\n```\n\n#### 5. Logging Configuration\n\n```json\n\"logConfiguration\": {\n  \"logDriver\": \"awslogs\",\n  \"options\": {\n    \"awslogs-group\": \"/ecs/mini-java-app\",\n    \"awslogs-region\": \"us-east-1\",\n    \"awslogs-stream-prefix\": \"ecs\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Register Task Definition\n\n```bash\naws ecs register-task-definition --cli-input-json file://ecs/task-definition.json\n```\n\n---\n\n## ECS Service Configuration\n\n### Key Components\n\n#### 1. Service Parameters\n\n```json\n\"serviceName\": \"mini-java-app-service\",\n\"taskDefinition\": \"mini-java-app-task\",\n\"desiredCount\": 2,\n\"launchType\": \"FARGATE\"\n```\n\n#### 2. Network Configuration (awsvpc)\n\n```json\n\"networkConfiguration\": {\n  \"awsvpcConfiguration\": {\n    \"subnets\": [\"subnet-xxx\", \"subnet-yyy\"],\n    \"securityGroups\": [\"sg-xxx\"],\n    \"assignPublicIp\": \"ENABLED\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Important Notes:**\n- **awsvpc** is the only network mode supported by Fargate\n- **assignPublicIp**: Set to \"ENABLED\" if tasks need internet access (e.g., to pull images from ECR)\n- Use at least 2 subnets in different Availability Zones for high availability\n\n#### 3. Load Balancer Configuration\n\n```json\n\"loadBalancers\": [\n  {\n    \"targetGroupArn\": \"arn:aws:elasticloadbalancing:...\",\n    \"containerName\": \"mini-java-app\",\n    \"containerPort\": 8080\n  }\n],\n\"healthCheckGracePeriodSeconds\": 300\n```\n\n**Note**: Target Group must use `target-type: ip` for Fargate.\n\n#### 4. Deployment Configuration\n\n```json\n\"deploymentConfiguration\": {\n  \"maximumPercent\": 200,\n  \"minimumHealthyPercent\": 50\n}\n```\n\n- **maximumPercent**: Allows rolling updates (200% = double capacity during deployment)\n- **minimumHealthyPercent**: Ensures availability during deployment\n\n#### 5. Service Tags\n\n```json\n\"tags\": [\n  {\"key\": \"Environment\", \"value\": \"production\"},\n  {\"key\": \"Application\", \"value\": \"mini-java-app\"}\n]\n```\n\n**IMPORTANT**: Use `tags` parameter, NOT `serviceTags` (which is invalid).\n\n---\n\n## Deploying to AWS ECS Fargate\n\n### Using Deployment Script (Recommended)\n\n#### Linux/macOS:\n\n```bash\nchmod +x scripts/deploy-image.sh\n./scripts/deploy-image.sh\n```\n\n#### Windows:\n\n```cmd\nscripts\\deploy-image.bat\n```\n\n### Manual Deployment Steps\n\n#### 1. Create ECS Cluster\n\n```bash\naws ecs create-cluster --cluster-name mini-java-app-cluster\n```\n\n#### 2. Register Task Definition\n\n```bash\naws ecs register-task-definition --cli-input-json file://ecs/task-definition.json\n```\n\n#### 3. Create Application Load Balancer (Optional)\n\n```bash\n# Create ALB\naws elbv2 create-load-balancer \\\n  --name mini-java-app-alb \\\n  --subnets subnet-xxx subnet-yyy \\\n  --security-groups sg-xxx \\\n  --scheme internet-facing \\\n  --type application\n\n# Create Target Group (target-type: ip for Fargate)\naws elbv2 create-target-group \\\n  --name mini-java-app-tg \\\n  --protocol HTTP \\\n  --port 8080 \\\n  --vpc-id vpc-xxx \\\n  --target-type ip \\\n  --health-check-path /mini-app/actuator/health\n\n# Create Listener\naws elbv2 create-listener \\\n  --load-balancer-arn <alb-arn> \\\n  --protocol HTTP \\\n  --port 80 \\\n  --default-actions Type=forward,TargetGroupArn=<tg-arn>\n```\n\n#### 4. Create ECS Service\n\n```bash\naws ecs create-service \\\n  --cluster mini-java-app-cluster \\\n  --service-name mini-java-app-service \\\n  --task-definition mini-java-app-task \\\n  --desired-count 2 \\\n  --launch-type FARGATE \\\n  --network-configuration \"awsvpcConfiguration={subnets=[subnet-xxx,subnet-yyy],securityGroups=[sg-xxx],assignPublicIp=ENABLED}\" \\\n  --load-balancers \"targetGroupArn=<tg-arn>,containerName=mini-java-app,containerPort=8080\" \\\n  --health-check-grace-period-seconds 300\n```\n\n#### 5. Wait for Service Stability\n\n```bash\naws ecs wait services-stable \\\n  --cluster mini-java-app-cluster \\\n  --services mini-java-app-service\n```\n\n---\n\n## Post-Deployment Verification\n\n### 1. Check Service Status\n\n```bash\naws ecs describe-services \\\n  --cluster mini-java-app-cluster \\\n  --services mini-java-app-service\n```\n\n### 2. List Running Tasks\n\n```bash\naws ecs list-tasks \\\n  --cluster mini-java-app-cluster \\\n  --service-name mini-java-app-service\n```\n\n### 3. Describe Task Details\n\n```bash\naws ecs describe-tasks \\\n  --cluster mini-java-app-cluster \\\n  --tasks <task-id>\n```\n\n### 4. Test Application Endpoint\n\n#### Without Load Balancer (using task public IP):\n\n```bash\n# Get task public IP\naws ecs describe-tasks \\\n  --cluster mini-java-app-cluster \\\n  --tasks <task-id> \\\n  --query 'tasks[0].attachments[0].details[?name==`networkInterfaceId`].value' \\\n  --output text | xargs -I {} aws ec2 describe-network-interfaces \\\n  --network-interface-ids {} \\\n  --query 'NetworkInterfaces[0].Association.PublicIp' \\\n  --output text\n\n# Test endpoint\ncurl http://<task-public-ip>:8080/mini-app\n```\n\n#### With Load Balancer:\n\n```bash\n# Get ALB DNS name\naws elbv2 describe-load-balancers \\\n  --names mini-java-app-alb \\\n  --query 'LoadBalancers[0].DNSName' \\\n  --output text\n\n# Test endpoint\ncurl http://<alb-dns-name>/mini-app\n```\n\n---\n\n## Monitoring and Logging\n\n### CloudWatch Logs\n\n#### View Logs in Real-Time\n\n```bash\naws logs tail /ecs/mini-java-app --follow\n```\n\n#### Query Specific Log Streams\n\n```bash\n# List log streams\naws logs describe-log-streams --log-group-name /ecs/mini-java-app\n\n# Get specific log stream\naws logs get-log-events \\\n  --log-group-name /ecs/mini-java-app \\\n  --log-stream-name ecs/mini-java-app/<task-id>\n```\n\n### CloudWatch Metrics\n\n#### View ECS Service Metrics\n\n```bash\n# CPU Utilization\naws cloudwatch get-metric-statistics \\\n  --namespace AWS/ECS \\\n  --metric-name CPUUtilization \\\n  --dimensions Name=ServiceName,Value=mini-java-app-service Name=ClusterName,Value=mini-java-app-cluster \\\n  --start-time 2023-01-01T00:00:00Z \\\n  --end-time 2023-01-02T00:00:00Z \\\n  --period 3600 \\\n  --statistics Average\n\n# Memory Utilization\naws cloudwatch get-metric-statistics \\\n  --namespace AWS/ECS \\\n  --metric-name MemoryUtilization \\\n  --dimensions Name=ServiceName,Value=mini-java-app-service Name=ClusterName,Value=mini-java-app-cluster \\\n  --start-time 2023-01-01T00:00:00Z \\\n  --end-time 2023-01-02T00:00:00Z \\\n  --period 3600 \\\n  --statistics Average\n```\n\n### CloudWatch Alarms\n\n```bash\n# Create CPU alarm\naws cloudwatch put-metric-alarm \\\n  --alarm-name mini-java-app-high-cpu \\\n  --alarm-description \"Alert when CPU exceeds 80%\" \\\n  --metric-name CPUUtilization \\\n  --namespace AWS/ECS \\\n  --statistic Average \\\n  --period 300 \\\n  --threshold 80 \\\n  --comparison-operator GreaterThanThreshold \\\n  --evaluation-periods 2 \\\n  --dimensions Name=ServiceName,Value=mini-java-app-service Name=ClusterName,Value=mini-java-app-cluster\n```\n\n---\n\n## Scaling and Management\n\n### Manual Scaling\n\n```bash\n# Scale up to 5 tasks\naws ecs update-service \\\n  --cluster mini-java-app-cluster \\\n  --service mini-java-app-service \\\n  --desired-count 5\n\n# Scale down to 1 task\naws ecs update-service \\\n  --cluster mini-java-app-cluster \\\n  --service mini-java-app-service \\\n  --desired-count 1\n```\n\n### Auto Scaling\n\n#### Register Scalable Target\n\n```bash\naws application-autoscaling register-scalable-target \\\n  --service-namespace ecs \\\n  --scalable-dimension ecs:service:DesiredCount \\\n  --resource-id service/mini-java-app-cluster/mini-java-app-service \\\n  --min-capacity 2 \\\n  --max-capacity 10\n```\n\n#### Create Scaling Policy (Target Tracking)\n\n```bash\n# CPU-based scaling\naws application-autoscaling put-scaling-policy \\\n  --service-namespace ecs \\\n  --scalable-dimension ecs:service:DesiredCount \\\n  --resource-id service/mini-java-app-cluster/mini-java-app-service \\\n  --policy-name cpu-scaling-policy \\\n  --policy-type TargetTrackingScaling \\\n  --target-tracking-scaling-policy-configuration file://scaling-policy.json\n```\n\n**scaling-policy.json:**\n\n```json\n{\n  \"TargetValue\": 70.0,\n  \"PredefinedMetricSpecification\": {\n    \"PredefinedMetricType\": \"ECSServiceAverageCPUUtilization\"\n  },\n  \"ScaleOutCooldown\": 60,\n  \"ScaleInCooldown\": 300\n}\n```\n\n### Update Service (Rolling Deployment)\n\n```bash\n# Force new deployment (e.g., after pushing new image with same tag)\naws ecs update-service \\\n  --cluster mini-java-app-cluster \\\n  --service mini-java-app-service \\\n  --force-new-deployment\n\n# Update task definition\naws ecs update-service \\\n  --cluster mini-java-app-cluster \\\n  --service mini-java-app-service \\\n  --task-definition mini-java-app-task:2\n```\n\n### Blue/Green Deployment\n\nFor blue/green deployments, use AWS CodeDeploy with ECS:\n\n```bash\n# Update service to use CODE_DEPLOY deployment controller\naws ecs create-service \\\n  --cluster mini-java-app-cluster \\\n  --service-name mini-java-app-service \\\n  --task-definition mini-java-app-task \\\n  --desired-count 2 \\\n  --launch-type FARGATE \\\n  --deployment-controller type=CODE_DEPLOY \\\n  --network-configuration \"awsvpcConfiguration={subnets=[subnet-xxx,subnet-yyy],securityGroups=[sg-xxx],assignPublicIp=ENABLED}\"\n```\n\n---\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### Common Issues\n\n#### 1. Task Fails to Start\n\n**Symptoms**: Tasks transition from PENDING to STOPPED immediately.\n\n**Troubleshooting Steps**:\n\n```bash\n# Describe stopped tasks\naws ecs describe-tasks \\\n  --cluster mini-java-app-cluster \\\n  --tasks <task-id> \\\n  --query 'tasks[0].stoppedReason'\n\n# Check task logs\naws logs tail /ecs/mini-java-app --since 1h\n```\n\n**Common Causes**:\n- Image pull failure (incorrect image URI, authentication issues)\n- Invalid task definition (CPU/memory combination, missing IAM roles)\n- Application startup failure\n\n#### 2. CannotPullContainerError\n\n**Error**: `CannotPullContainerError: Error response from daemon`\n\n**Solutions**:\n- Verify image URI is correct\n- Ensure `ecsTaskExecutionRole` has ECR permissions\n- Check ECR repository permissions\n- Verify tasks have internet access (NAT Gateway or public IP)\n\n```bash\n# Test ECR access\naws ecr get-login-password --region us-east-1 | docker login --username AWS --password-stdin <account-id>.dkr.ecr.us-east-1.amazonaws.com\n\n# Check image exists\naws ecr describe-images --repository-name mini-java-app\n```\n\n#### 3. Task Network Issues\n\n**Symptoms**: Tasks start but cannot communicate with external services.\n\n**Troubleshooting Steps**:\n- Verify security group allows outbound traffic\n- Check subnet route tables (need route to Internet Gateway or NAT Gateway)\n- Verify DNS resolution\n\n```bash\n# Check security group rules\naws ec2 describe-security-groups --group-ids sg-xxx\n\n# Check route tables\naws ec2 describe-route-tables --filters \"Name=association.subnet-id,Values=subnet-xxx\"\n```\n\n#### 4. Invalid CPU or Memory Configuration\n\n**Error**: `Invalid CPU or memory value specified`\n\n**Solution**: Use valid Fargate CPU/memory combinations:\n\n| CPU | Valid Memory Values |\n|-----|---------------------|\n| 256 | 512, 1024, 2048 |\n| 512 | 1024, 2048, 3072, 4096 |\n| 1024 | 2048, 3072, 4096, 5120, 6144, 7168, 8192 |\n| 2048 | 4096-16384 (increments of 1024) |\n| 4096 | 8192-30720 (increments of 1024) |\n\n#### 5. Service Fails Health Checks\n\n**Symptoms**: Tasks start but are marked unhealthy and replaced.\n\n**Troubleshooting Steps**:\n- Verify health check endpoint is accessible\n- Check application logs for startup errors\n- Increase `healthCheckGracePeriodSeconds` if application takes long to start\n\n```bash\n# Test health check endpoint from within VPC\ncurl http://<task-ip>:8080/mini-app/actuator/health\n\n# Check target group health\naws elbv2 describe-target-health --target-group-arn <tg-arn>\n```\n\n#### 6. Application Logs Not Appearing\n\n**Troubleshooting Steps**:\n- Verify log group exists\n- Check `ecsTaskExecutionRole` has CloudWatch Logs permissions\n- Verify log configuration in task definition\n\n```bash\n# Check log group\naws logs describe-log-groups --log-group-name-prefix /ecs/mini-java-app\n\n# Check IAM role permissions\naws iam get-role-policy --role-name ecsTaskExecutionRole --policy-name CloudWatchLogsPolicy\n```\n\n### Debugging Commands\n\n```bash\n# Get task events\naws ecs describe-services \\\n  --cluster mini-java-app-cluster \\\n  --services mini-java-app-service \\\n  --query 'services[0].events[:5]'\n\n# Get task stopped reason\naws ecs describe-tasks \\\n  --cluster mini-java-app-cluster \\\n  --tasks <task-id> \\\n  --query 'tasks[0].stoppedReason'\n\n# Check container exit code\naws ecs describe-tasks \\\n  --cluster mini-java-app-cluster \\\n  --tasks <task-id> \\\n  --query 'tasks[0].containers[0].exitCode'\n```\n\n---\n\n## Security Best Practices\n\n### 1. Use Least Privilege IAM Roles\n\n```json\n{\n  \"Version\": \"2012-10-17\",\n  \"Statement\": [\n    {\n      \"Effect\": \"Allow\",\n      \"Action\": [\n        \"ecr:GetAuthorizationToken\",\n        \"ecr:BatchCheckLayerAvailability\",\n        \"ecr:GetDownloadUrlForLayer\",\n        \"ecr:BatchGetImage\"\n      ],\n      \"Resource\": \"*\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"Effect\": \"Allow\",\n      \"Action\": [\n        \"logs:CreateLogStream\",\n        \"logs:PutLogEvents\"\n      ],\n      \"Resource\": \"arn:aws:logs:*:*:log-group:/ecs/mini-java-app:*\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n### 2. Secure Environment Variables\n\nUse AWS Secrets Manager or Systems Manager Parameter Store for sensitive data:\n\n```json\n\"secrets\": [\n  {\n    \"name\": \"DB_PASSWORD\",\n    \"valueFrom\": \"arn:aws:secretsmanager:us-east-1:123456789:secret:db-password\"\n  }\n]\n```\n\n### 3. Enable Container Insights\n\n```bash\naws ecs update-cluster-settings \\\n  --cluster mini-java-app-cluster \\\n  --settings name=containerInsights,value=enabled\n```\n\n### 4. Use Private Subnets with NAT Gateway\n\nFor production workloads, use private subnets:\n\n```bash\n# Create NAT Gateway in public subnet\naws ec2 create-nat-gateway \\\n  --subnet-id <public-subnet-id> \\\n  --allocation-id <eip-allocation-id>\n\n# Update private subnet route table\naws ec2 create-route \\\n  --route-table-id <private-rt-id> \\\n  --destination-cidr-block 0.0.0.0/0 \\\n  --nat-gateway-id <nat-gw-id>\n\n# Update service network configuration\n\"awsvpcConfiguration\": {\n  \"subnets\": [\"<private-subnet-1>\", \"<private-subnet-2>\"],\n  \"securityGroups\": [\"<sg-id>\"],\n  \"assignPublicIp\": \"DISABLED\"\n}\n```\n\n### 5. Enable ECR Image Scanning\n\n```bash\naws ecr put-image-scanning-configuration \\\n  --repository-name mini-java-app \\\n  --image-scanning-configuration scanOnPush=true\n\n# View scan findings\naws ecr describe-image-scan-findings \\\n  --repository-name mini-java-app \\\n  --image-id imageTag=latest\n```\n\n### 6. Restrict Security Group Rules\n\n```bash\n# Allow traffic only from ALB\naws ec2 authorize-security-group-ingress \\\n  --group-id <task-sg-id> \\\n  --protocol tcp \\\n  --port 8080 \\\n  --source-group <alb-sg-id>\n```\n\n### 7. Enable VPC Flow Logs\n\n```bash\naws ec2 create-flow-logs \\\n  --resource-type VPC \\\n  --resource-ids <vpc-id> \\\n  --traffic-type ALL \\\n  --log-destination-type cloud-watch-logs \\\n  --log-group-name /aws/vpc/flowlogs\n```\n\n---\n\n## Additional Resources\n\n- [AWS ECS Fargate Documentation](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/AWS_Fargate.html)\n- [ECS Task Definition Parameters](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/task_definition_parameters.html)\n- [Fargate Task Networking](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/fargate-task-networking.html)\n- [Spring Boot in Containers](https://spring.io/guides/gs/spring-boot-docker/)\n- [Java in Containers](https://www.eclipse.org/openj9/docs/xxusecontainersupport/)\n\n---\n\n## Support\n\nFor issues or questions:\n1. Check CloudWatch logs: `aws logs tail /ecs/mini-java-app --follow`\n2. Review ECS service events: `aws ecs describe-services --cluster mini-java-app-cluster --services mini-java-app-service`\n3. Consult AWS ECS documentation\n4. Contact your DevOps team or AWS Support\n\n---\n\n**Document Version**: 1.0  \n**Last Updated**: 2025-12-12  \n**Maintained By**: DevOps Team"
